SUMMARY:Photography Social Networking Event
LOCATION:1630 East 7th Avenue Tampa \, FL 33605 United States
DESCRIPTION:Looking to meet fellow photographers\, creatives\, and people 
 who love the arts? Join us at the Florida Museum of Photographic Arts for 
 a relaxed evening of conversation\, connection\, and community. Doors open
  and the event begins at 6:00 PM\, giving you time to mingle and connect b
 efore we kick things off with a guided tour of our current exhibitions at 
 6:30 PM. Explore whats on view\, learn more about the artists and their wo
 rk\, and then stick around to continue the conversation. Whether youre a p
 rofessional photographer\, just getting started\, work in the arts\, or si
 mply have a passion for photography and museums\, youre welcome. Come meet
  new people\, exchange ideas\, discover creative opportunities\, and conne
 ct with Tampa Bays vibrant arts community in a casual and welcoming settin
 g. Bring a business card\, share your social media\, or simply come as you
  are. All experience levels and backgrounds are welcome! \n\nPermalink: ht
 tps://www.tampa.gov/node/194961
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/194961
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ee74220b-537c-47bf-b868-cc0a34d313d2
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20261022T000542Z
DTSTART:20261023T220000Z
DTEND:20261024T010000Z
SUMMARY:16mm Microcinema Friday Night
LOCATION:211 South Howard Ave Tampa \, FL 33606 United States
DESCRIPTION:CINEMA SOCIAL For Film Lovers\, Analog Fans the Cinematically 
 Curious The Glow of Real Film. In Real Life.Think of this evening as a cur
 ated in-real-life experience. A three hour pop-up cinema party. Interestin
 g and unusual short films\, animations and music\, followed by a feature f
 ilm. But more. Intermissions to mingle\, and time after the feature to con
 nect with other discuss what you have seen. Before streaming\, before digi
 tal\, there was the flicker of light through celluloid. 16mm Microcinema N
 ight at The Paper Seahorse is an immersive experience bringing back the ma
 gic of real film projection in an intimate screening room where the whir o
 f the projector becomes part of the show. Film has a warmth and texture th
 at screens cant quite capture: the grain\, the glow\, the small imperfecti
 ons that remind you youre watching something physical and alive. Settle in
  with fellow film lovers for an evening of curated shorts\, animation and 
 a feature presentation\, shared the way cinema was meant to be experienced
 : together\, in the dark. This Month: The Opening Act. The evening begins 
 with a variety of shorts: music to set the mood\, followed by a selection 
 of vintage animation and short films. Feature Presentation: David and Lisa
  (1962). Directed by Frank Perry\, this small\, independent black-and-whit
 e film became a surprise sensation and earned Academy Award nominations fo
 r Best Director and Best Adapted Screenplay. Keir Dullea (2001: A Space Od
 yssey) stars as David\, a brilliant teenager living in a residential treat
 ment center who cannot bear to be touched. There he meets Lisa (Janet Marg
 olin)\, a young woman who speaks only in rhyme. As the two slowly find the
 ir way toward each other\, the film becomes a tender\, deeply human story 
 about fear\, trust\, and the courage it takes to connect. Decades before i
 t was common for films to portray mental health with honesty and compassio
 n David and Lisa did just that\, and its warmth still feels remarkably fre
 sh. Pre-packaged local food\, curated snacks\, soft drinks\, and mocktails
  are available at the concession. 6:00 to 9:00 p.m. \n\nPermalink: https:/
 /www.tampa.gov/node/196616
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/196616
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8ad6a59d-6d11-4918-ba7b-bfc391e08dde
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20261022T000542Z
DTSTART:20261023T130000Z
DTEND:20261023T200000Z
SUMMARY:Compost Giveaway
LOCATION:3100 N Ola Ave Tampa \, FL 33602-2509 United States
DESCRIPTION:Get 30 gallons of FREE compost to level up your gardening save
  water. Learn about compost\, topdressing\, and keeping your lawn healthy.
  Join us for our Compost Giveaway event at Plymouth Playground! Get FREE c
 ompost on: Friday\, October 23\, 2026 from 9am to 4pm Saturday\, October 2
 4\, 2026 at 9am  If supplies are available City of Tampa Utilities custome
 rs can register to load up and take 30 gallons of high-quality compost . O
 ur goal is to help improve your soils ability to hold water and give your 
 lawn or landscape the boost it needs to thrive in every season. Not only i
 s compost a great tool for gardening\, but it also helps you save water ! 
 Topdressing with compost will increase your soils water holding capacity a
 nd help sustain your lawn or landscape through the dry spring season. Reme
 mber\, the City of Tampa is under once-a-week watering (https:www.tampa.go
 vwaterrestrictions) restrictions. Let us help you keep your lawn or landsc
 ape healthy\, while keeping your water use down. What you need to know: Re
 ad review the information provided on compost topdressing. Arrive at the l
 ocation at your designated time. Bring your own container: 5-gallon bucket
 s work best! Take up to 30 gallons of compost (or six 5-gallon buckets) . 
 \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa.gov/node/196581
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/196581
END:VEVENT
