SUMMARY:Nell Ward Lecture: Making Sense of the Wild Frontier
LOCATION:801 Water Street Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Making Sense of the Wild Frontier: Early Survey Work in Florid
 a\, 1821-1880 Featuring historian Joe Knetsch\, Ph.D. Join us this year in
  October for our annual Nell Ward Lecture. Historian Joe Knetsch will take
  the audience back to 19th-century Florida\, a wild place where the absenc
 e of details and facts was replaced by mystery and legends. A small but de
 dicated corps of surveyors brought order to the land of alligators and swa
 mps\, tasked with the almost impossible job of evenly partitioning the lan
 d. Those early surveys survive to this day and are the basis of all land t
 ransactions in the state. Time: Doors open at 6:00 p.m.\\\; Program at 6:3
 0 p.m. Location: TECO Hall (2nd floor) at the History Center Parking: Free
  valet parking will be provided. Stay for a book signing following the tal
 k. The Nell Ward Lecture is an annual special lecture\, free and open to t
 he public\, offering a fascinating journey through cartography\, explorati
 on and history. About the lecturer: Joe Knetsch served as historian for th
 e Division of State Lands at the Florida Department of Environmental Prote
 ction for 28 years. He earned a Ph.D. in history from Florida State Univer
 sity. He has authored and edited 16 books\, mostly on Florida history\, an
 d more than 200 published articles on history. He has also written more th
 an 40 book reviews for national magazines. Knetsch has served on the edito
 rial boards of several magazines\, including Tampa Bay History and El Escr
 ibano. He has also served on the boards of the St. Augustine Historical So
 ciety\, the Broward Historical Commission\, the Tallahassee Historical Soc
 iety and the Florida Historical Society. He lives in Tallahassee with his 
 wife of 50 years\, Linda\, and their four cats. \n\nPermalink: https://www
 .tampa.gov/node/196196
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/196196
END:VEVENT
